00:15:35.212 --> 00:15:36.420
Exactly as you would-- right.

00:15:36.420 --> 00:15:39.770
So there's plenty in there.

00:15:39.770 --> 00:15:41.410
CHRIS SMITH: Oh.

00:15:41.410 --> 00:15:43.390
NE-- or EQ.

00:15:43.390 --> 00:15:44.070
Yes.

00:15:44.070 --> 00:15:45.670
PowerShell semantics, yo.

00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:48.010
JOHN SKEET: Yo, I'm not
a PowerShell developer.

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:50.500
So now we see all the C# books.

00:15:50.500 --> 00:15:53.080
CHRIS SMITH: And this is all
just standard PowerShell.

00:15:53.080 --> 00:15:55.275
You can use these today.

00:15:55.275 --> 00:15:55.900
It's all great.

00:15:55.900 --> 00:15:56.710
